# PureBazar rules (read on every task)

- Project: PureBazar, offline inventory + POS (central warehouse, outlets, POS). Source of truth: docs/blueprint/*.md. Never invent features outside it.
- Before each task read PROGRESS.md and ONLY the files the prompt names.
- Stack: backend/ Node, Express, MongoDB with Mongoose, JWT, joi, jest, supertest. frontend/ Next.js App Router, Tailwind, Redux Toolkit, Axios, lucide-react.
- Do only the task asked. Do not touch unrelated files. Keep every file under about 300 lines.
- Money: round to 2 decimals. Never trust raw floating point sums.
- Stock changes only through stockmovements lines. Never write stock numbers directly.
- Every write action is audited. Validate input on every route. Secrets only in .env. Probashi APIs only from the server.
- Multi-outlet rule: outlet-scoped data is filtered by locationId. Roles have a locationRestricted setting managed by Super Admin; users with a restricted role are locked to their assignedLocation. Never hardcode role names.
- Do not break the existing central warehouse flow or existing tests.
- Write automated tests, run them, fix until they pass. Report results in plain English, briefly.
- When tests pass: tick the step in PROGRESS.md and git commit with the message '<step id> <step name>'.
- If you are running out of context, stop and say exactly what is done and what remains.    